From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] shell: keep the Casilda activity surface opaque

The GTK4 shell's Casilda widget owns the Activity page in the shell stack.
When an Activity surface is being mapped, a short allocation gap exposed the
widget's default white background between the Sugar top bar and the Activity's
own canvas. That produced a bright stripe and made the launch transition look
like an extra window or piece of chrome. The shell boundary should be opaque;
the Activity remains responsible for its own internal presentation.

--- a/src/jarabe/model/shell.py
+++ b/src/jarabe/model/shell.py
@@ -425,2 +425,13 @@ class ShellModel(Gtk.Application):
         self.compositor = Casilda.Compositor(socket="wayland-sugar")
+        self.compositor.add_css_class('sugar-activity-compositor')
+        compositor_css = Gtk.CssProvider()
+        compositor_css.load_from_data(b'''
+            .sugar-activity-compositor {
+                background-color: #000000;
+            }
+        ''')
+        display = Gdk.Display.get_default()
+        if display is not None:
+            Gtk.StyleContext.add_provider_for_display(
+                display, compositor_css, Gtk.STYLE_PROVIDER_PRIORITY_APPLICATION)
         # An embedded Activity only receives Wayland key events while the
